; Gran Turismo 2 (USA) (Simulation Mode) (Rev 1) [SCUS-94488] - v1.1 cheats derived by GT2Recomp
; The community "Simulation Disc" cheats in DuckStation's cheats.zip are for the
; v1.0 / v1.2 pressings. On v1.1 the save/profile structure sits 0x370 bytes
; higher (base 0x801C96B0 instead of 0x801C9340), so every data code below is
; the community code shifted by +0x370; the code-patch sites were checked
; instruction by instruction against the v1.1 GT-mode overlay. Every entry
; here was run on the v1.1 Simulation disc in the lab with a screenshot of the
; result - see docs/CHEAT_VERIFICATION.md. Guarded (A4) on a word of the
; GT-mode menu overlay that no cheat touches, so nothing is written while the
; race overlay (or, on the Combined Disc, arcade mode) occupies that memory.

[A Ton Of Cash]
Author = community (DuckStation cheats.zip, v1.0/v1.2), re-derived for v1.1 by GT2Recomp
Description = Credits held at 99,999,999 while in the GT-mode menus (the v1.0 code wrote 0x801D0FC8, dead memory on v1.1; the v1.1 credits word is 0x801D1338 = profile 0 + 0x4014).
Type = Gameshark
Activation = EndFrame
A4017A3C 00741823
901D1338 05F5E0FF
00000000 FFFF

[Money Never Decreases]
Author = community (DuckStation cheats.zip, v1.0/v1.2), re-derived for v1.1 by GT2Recomp
Description = The two purchase paths store the reduced balance with sw v1,0x4014(sN); both stores become no-ops (the community code's 0x2400 halfword, on the same instructions at the same addresses on v1.1). Restored when the cheat is switched off.
Type = Gameshark
Activation = EndFrame
A4017A3C 00741823
A7017A42 AE232400
A7017D4A AE432400
00000000 FFFF

[Any Car Can Play Any Circuit]
Author = community (DuckStation cheats.zip, v1.0/v1.2), re-derived for v1.1 by GT2Recomp
Description = The horsepower-limit check at 0x800148E0 (beq v0,v1,+0xC) becomes an unconditional branch, the community patch on the identical v1.1 instruction. Restored when switched off.
